MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Arrival felt like a plausible next choice because my Star Trek interaction suggests some interest in science fiction and encounters with unfamiliar life.",
    "Its thoughtful alien-contact premise gave me a specific reason to try it, although one visible Star Trek interaction is only a limited clue to my tastes."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Suicide Squad and Aquaman did not appeal to me now because superhero action does not carry the same appeal as the alien-contact story that drew me to Arrival.",
    "For the unidentified items, I could not establish a connection to my interests; passing on them does not mean I would dislike their actual content."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seemed to stretch a possible interest in science fiction into an interest in superhero adventures.",
    "A broad resemblance between imagined worlds was not enough to make every recognizable title feel relevant to me."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The distinction between thoughtful encounters with unfamiliar life and superhero action mattered to my choice today.",
    "Most of my history is unidentified, so my single recognizable Star Trek interaction leaves substantial uncertainty about what else I would enjoy."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "Arrival connected plausibly with my limited visible science-fiction interest, while the superhero choices extended that clue further than my current preferences supported."
}
